### VShop API — try these in IntelliJ (HTTP Client) or copy into Postman.
### Android emulator reaches your PC at http://10.0.2.2:8080

@base = http://localhost:8080
@token = paste-accessToken-from-login
@refresh = paste-refreshToken-from-login

### 1. Register -> 201 { "id": "1", "email": "vy@example.com" } (no tokens: log in next)
POST {{base}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "vy@example.com", "password": "password123" }

### 2. Login -> copy "accessToken" into @token and "refreshToken" into @refresh above
POST {{base}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "vy@example.com", "password": "password123" }

### 2a. Who am I (needs the access token; 401 when it's missing or expired)
GET {{base}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 2b. Refresh -> new accessToken + refreshToken. The old refresh token stops working (401 if reused)
POST {{base}}/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{refresh}}" }

### 2c. Profile name + phone (used as payer details for PayWay)
PUT {{base}}/api/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fullName": "Vy Sengchhay", "phone": "012345678" }

### 3. Categories (public)
GET {{base}}/api/categories

### 4. Products (public): filters are optional
GET {{base}}/api/products?categoryId=1&q=coffee&sort=price_asc&page=0&size=20

### 5. Product detail
GET {{base}}/api/products/1

### 6. Add an address
POST {{base}}/api/addresses
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Vy Sengchhay", "phone": "012345678",
  "province": "Phnom Penh", "district": "Khan Chamkarmon", "commune": "Sangkat Tuol Tumpung Ti Muoy",
  "street": "#12, St 450", "note": "Near the market", "isDefault": true
}

### 7. Create order from cart (prices are calculated on the server)
POST {{base}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "addressId": 1, "items": [ { "productId": 1, "quantity": 1 }, { "productId": 4, "quantity": 2 } ] }

### 8. Start payment -> returns qrString + abapayDeeplink + tranId
POST {{base}}/api/orders/1/pay
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 9. Poll status (the app calls this every 3 s)
GET {{base}}/api/orders/1/payment-status
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 10. MOCK MODE ONLY: pretend the customer paid (use tranId from step 8)
POST {{base}}/api/dev/payments/PASTE_TRAN_ID/approve

### 11. My orders
GET {{base}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 12. Cancel an unpaid order
POST {{base}}/api/orders/1/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ---------- Password reset ----------

### 13. Request a code -> the 6-digit code is emailed to Mailpit: open http://localhost:8025
POST {{base}}/api/auth/password-reset/request
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "vy@example.com" }

### 14. Verify the code (optional check, doesn't use the code up)
POST {{base}}/api/auth/password-reset/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "vy@example.com", "otp": "PASTE_CODE_FROM_MAILPIT" }

### 15. Set the new password (logs out every device: all refresh tokens are revoked)
POST {{base}}/api/auth/password-reset/confirm
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "vy@example.com", "otp": "PASTE_CODE_FROM_MAILPIT", "newPassword": "newpassword123" }

### ---------- Logout ----------

### 16. Logout -> { "message": "Logged out" } (safe to call twice)
POST {{base}}/api/auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{refresh}}" }
